<title>FINLAND: ICE HOCKEY-WORLD CHAMPIONSHIP RESULTS.</title>
<headline>ICE HOCKEY-WORLD CHAMPIONSHIP RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-05-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results at the ice hockey world</p>
<p>championship on Saturday:</p>
<p>Pool B</p>
<p>In Turku: Canada 6 Italy 0 (2-0 3-0 1-0)</p>
<p>Scorers: Jeff Friesen (06:21), Keith Primeau (14:00), Travis</p>
<p>Green (25:13), Owen Nolan (30:47), Bob Errey (37:51), Dean</p>
<p>Evason (47:19)</p>
<p>Penalties: Canada 4 minutes, Italy 2</p>
<p>Attendance: 5,250</p>
<p>Pool A</p>
<p>In Helsinki: France 3 Czech Republic 9 (3-2 0-3 0-4)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>France - Philippe Bozon (10:54, 18:29), Christian Pouget</p>
<p>(19:32)</p>
<p>Czech Republic - Jiri Vykoukal (11:21), David Vyborny</p>
<p>(15:24, 21:28), Robert Lang (32:56), Pavel Patera (34:19),</p>
<p>Robert Reichel (49:11), Martin Prochazka (50:50, 54:15),</p>
<p>Vladimir Ujcic (55:53).</p>
<p>Penalties: France 4 minutes, Czech Republic 2</p>
<p>Attendance: 12,806</p>
